  <XDFTABLE uniqueid="0x10B5" flags="0x0">
    <title>IAP - Neutral/Clutch-In | Cyl 1</title>
    <description>CORRECTED LABEL (v2, code-confirmed): the GSX-R fuel bank has only 8 IAP (30x50) + 8 TPS (26x50) maps - no blend/spare maps like the Hayabusa (28+28). All 16 sit in ONE pointer array at 0x1560E4 (8 IAP then 8 TPS, each split 4 In-Gear + 4 Neutral/Clutch in array order). Confirmed: the TPS In-Gear maps are read by the in-gear base-fuel lookup FUN_0004536C and the Neutral maps by the neutral finaliser FUN_0004543E, which selects the neutral block on the neutral/clutch flag 0xFEF0271D bit0 (vacuum &gt;= ~0 kPa, RPM below gate) - the same shared code the Hayabusa uses; Z-data decode independently shows 4 cylinders x 2 conditions. So In-Gear vs Neutral/Clutch and the type (IAP/TPS) are code-proven; only the exact cylinder NUMBER within each group of four is by position. Values are GSX-R-specific - verify on a bench.

X: 30 pts 64.00..0.00 vacuum kPa; Y: 50 pts 800..16000 RPM
INPUTS (Hayabusa decompile): X = intake pressure (IAP); Y = engine RPM. Read by FUN_00045320.
MIN/MAX (32990-48L30): min 392, max 3195 raw (inj. time?).
REFERENCE: descriptor @0x1571E4, data @0x15DAF4, X @0x1571A8, Y @0x15DA90.</description>
