  <XDFTABLE uniqueid="0x1209" flags="0x0">
    <title>Steering Damper :: Damping vs Speed - Mode 1</title>
    <description>ELECTRONIC STEERING DAMPER modulation curve (decompile-confirmed). X axis = rear-wheel speed 0xFEBF63F4: raw 2560 = 20 km/h, so the 16 breakpoints are 0,20,40,...,300 km/h. Output = damping modulation (stock: 0 below ~60 km/h, rising to ~0x4000 = full at 300 km/h = light steering at low speed, firm at high speed). Three mode curves (1/2/3) selected by 0xFEBF6480. Read by FUN_00078006; feeds the PWM solenoid on T54 via FUN_00024cb4 (ch 0x500). This is the "steering damper map" that commercial tools edit; set the enable byte 0x172F28 to 0x00 to disable the damper entirely.

PORTED FROM HAYABUSA 5JCZSJ10 (HIGH: breakpoints byte-identical, almost certainly the same map). Units/scaling carried over; GSX-R addresses &amp; values are this read's own. Hayabusa code refs are not verified on GSX-R.
X: 16 pts 0..300 km/h
GSX-R TRACED INPUTS (from this ECU's lookup calls): X = 0xFEBF63F4 (engine RPM (500-8000 rpm)).
INPUTS (Hayabusa decompile): X = throttle position. Read by FUN_0006a926.
MIN/MAX (32990-48L30): min 0, max 16351 raw.
REFERENCE: descriptor @0x1716AC, data @0x171344, X @0x171324.</description>
